		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=16107#p16107"><![CDATA[
It is a good idea to add (de)serialization to Bullet. I've been looking into this for a while, and I'm planning to provide some solution soon.<br><br>Let's add serialize and deserialize methods (similar to irrlicht for example), and provide a basic binary chunk format that is backward/forward compatible (based on the <a href="http://www.martinreddy.net/gfx/2d/IFF.txt" class="postlink">iff format</a> but adding support for little/bit endian and 32bit/64bit similar to the <a href="http://www.atmind.nl/blender/mystery_ot_blend.html" class="postlink">Blender .blend format</a>).<br><a href="http://code.google.com/p/bullet/issues/detail?id=308" class="postlink">http://code.google.com/p/bullet/issues/detail?id=308</a><br><br>If you are running into issues on your side, please just make the members protected for now,<br>Thanks,<br>Erwin<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Tue Nov 17, 2009 7:54 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
